<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baijnath, Uttarakhand</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baijnath is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gomti-river">Gomti River</a> in Bageshwar district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttarakhand">Uttarakhand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, known for a group of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> temples. It is usually identified with Kartikeyapura, capital of the Katyuri kings, in the Katyur valley. The temples, of the 12th and 13th centuries, are protected monuments.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baijnath-uttarakhand.jpg" alt="Baijnath, Uttarakhand" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shikharsaxena1618 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baijnath_Dham_with_Himalayas_in_the_backdrop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
